Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Silica melts the compass
- Story & Context: Kael discovers a deactivated substation in the Salt Barrens, but the moment he touches the central relay, the machine begins to scream in high-frequency feedback that sounds like the earth weeping. "The map is a puddle under our feet" sings Kael as the group realizes their guiding synthesizer has finally short-circuited forever.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A macro shot of a compass needle dissolving into liquid gold, vibrant yellow light spilling across a cracked desert floor, dark and grainy aesthetic.

Track 2: Sift-Logic
- Story & Context: The caravan stops at the Obsidian Ridge, where the village elder, Zora, admits she has been hiding a secret transmitter inside her own glass jewelry. As she confesses to the caravan that she sent their coordinates to the wasteland raiders, she drops a heavy, iron-bound cowbell that shatters against the rocks. "Listen to the clicking of the metal teeth" she mutters, her voice lost in the sudden onset of a grit-storm.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a person wearing elaborate, jagged glass jewelry that refracts a dying sunset, sharp focus on the dust particles floating in the air like fallen stars.

Track 3: The furnace breathes a prayer
- Story & Context: Years after the migration has ended, the legend of the glass caravan persists in the city-states, told as a ghost story about a people who became so obsessed with their salvaged machines that they eventually merged with the sound. Even now, if you hold a piece of broken desert glass to your ear, you can hear the faint, lingering rhythm of a rimshot that refuses to stop. "We are the smoke that stays behind to sing" remains the final, haunting refrain of the myth.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A sprawling landscape of jagged, translucent glass dunes stretching into a violet sky, a single, lonely synth-oscillator resting atop a dune, glowing with an inner, dying warmth.

